      "content": "But we aren't talking about hypothetical \"unforeseen consequences,\" we're talking about real-world intelligence. If the intelligence shows with high probability that an authoritarian regime is about to consolidate power and start a genocide, isn't it actually unethical to just sit by and watch? To say \"we don't know for sure\" feels like a way to avoid the moral obligation to protect human rights. At what point does inaction become the immoral choice?",
